  "result": "Excellent! All 105 tests pass. I've successfully implemented customer tier-based discounts for the invoicing system:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/customers.js`** - Added export:\n   - `TIER_DISCOUNTS` object with discount percentages by tier:\n     - gold: 5%\n     - silver: 2.5%\n     - standard: 0%\n\n2. **`src/invoices.js`** - Updated two functions:\n   - `createInvoice()` - Now applies tier discount when line has no explicit `discountPercent`\n   - `addLine()` - Now applies tier discount to new lines when no explicit `discountPercent`\n   - Both respect explicit discount values (even 0) over tier defaults\n\n3. **Test updates:**\n   - Updated existing tests to account for tier discounts being automatically applied\n   - Added 16 new tests for tier discount functionality covering:\n     - Each tier applying the correct discount\n     - Explicit discounts overriding tier discounts\n     - Mixed scenarios with both tier and explicit discounts\n     - addLine behavior with tier discounts\n\n**Key behavior:**\n- When creating/adding lines without explicit `discountPercent`, the customer's tier discount is used\n- When `discountPercent` is explicitly provided (including 0), it takes priority over tier discount\n- Tier discount is looked up once from `TIER_DISCOUNTS` and applied to all eligible lines\n- All 105 tests pass (11 existing + 49 invoicing + 10 numbering + 6 issuance + 13 render + 16 tier discount)",
